INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'luke' AND c.chapter_number = 19 AND v.verse_number = 10), 'gathering', 'The gathering', 'Come to seek and to save that which was lost', $card$*And Yahusha (Jesus) said unto him, This day is salvation come to this house, forsomuch as he also is a son of Abraham. For the Son of Adam is come to seek and to save that which was lost.* (Luke 19:9-10)

*I will seek that which was lost, and bring again that which was driven away, and will bind up that which was broken, and will strengthen that which was sick: but I will destroy the fat and the strong; I will feed them with judgment.* (Ezekiel 34:16)

In Ezekiel, Yahuah (God) speaks in the first person: *I will seek that which was lost.* In Jericho, the Son of Adam says he *is come* to do exactly that — no citation formula, no as-it-is-written. The promise is simply re-spoken as his own errand.

And the verse before tells you what was found: salvation comes to Zacchaeus's house *forsomuch as he also is a son of Abraham.* The lost being sought and saved are the seed — a son of Abraham recovered to his own inheritance.$card$, '{"Ezekiel 34:16","Luke 19:9-10"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
