INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'john' AND c.chapter_number = 6 AND v.verse_number = 44), 'grace', 'Grace', 'Except the Father draw him — with lovingkindness have I drawn thee', $card$*No man can come to me, except the Father which hath sent me draw him: and I will raise him up at the last day.* (John 6:44)

*Yahuah (LORD) hath appeared of old unto me, saying, Yea, I have loved thee with an everlasting love: therefore with lovingkindness have I drawn thee.* (Jeremiah 31:3)

*Hear the word of Yahuah (LORD), O ye nations, and declare it in the isles afar off, and say, He that scattered Yashar'el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock.* (Jeremiah 31:10)

Draw is not a new word. It is the Father's own first-person covenant word, spoken of old to Yashar'el (Israel): with lovingkindness have I drawn thee. And the same chapter tells the nations and the isles afar off what the drawing is — he that scattered Yashar'el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock.

The drawing and the gathering are one act. No one comes except the Father draws, because the coming is the scattered being pulled home by the everlasting love that never let them go. Grace is the cord in the Father's hand.$card$, '{"Jeremiah 31:3, 10","John 6:44"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
