INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'john' AND c.chapter_number = 7 AND v.verse_number = 37), 'grace', 'Grace', 'If any man thirst — the waters were already poured for Jacob''s seed', $card$*In the last day, that great day of the feast, Yahusha (Jesus) stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink. He that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water.* (John 7:37-38)

*Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters, and he that hath no money; come ye, buy, and eat; yea, come, buy wine and milk without money and without price.* (Isaiah 55:1)

*Yet now hear, O Jacob my servant; and Yashar'el (Israel), whom I have chosen: Thus saith Yahuah (LORD) that made thee, and formed thee from the womb, which will help thee; Fear not, O Jacob, my servant; and thou, Jesurun, whom I have chosen. For I will pour water upon him that is thirsty, and floods upon the dry ground: I will pour my spirit upon thy seed, and my blessing upon thine offspring:* (Isaiah 44:1-3)

On the last great day of the feast he stands and cries an invitation Isaiah had already cried: Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters — without money and without price. The drink is free. That is grace, spoken centuries before in the same voice.

And the second oracle names who the water was promised to: hear, O Jacob my servant; I will pour my spirit upon thy seed, and my blessing upon thine offspring. The rivers of living water are the Spirit poured on the seed of Ya'aqov (Jacob) — the thirsty, scattered offspring the prophets never stopped addressing.$card$, '{"Isaiah 55:1","Isaiah 44:1-3","John 7:37-38"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
