INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = '1-john' AND c.chapter_number = 2 AND v.verse_number = 7), 'teaching', 'The teaching', 'No new commandment — the old one ye had from the beginning', $card$*Brethren, I write no new commandment unto you, but an old commandment which ye had from the beginning. The old commandment is the word which ye have heard from the beginning. Again, a new commandment I write unto you, which thing is true in him and in you: because the darkness is past, and the true light now shineth.* (1 John 2:7-8)

*And thou shalt love Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy might. And these words, which I command thee this day, shall be in thine heart:* (Deuteronomy 6:5-6)

*Thou shalt not avenge, nor bear any grudge against the children of thy people, but thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* (Leviticus 19:18)

The apostle says it himself, plainer than any argument: I write no new commandment unto you, but an old commandment which ye had from the beginning. The word heard from the beginning is Moses' word — love Yahuah (God) with all the heart, and love thy neighbour as thyself. Both commandments were already in the Torah, and the Torah said the words shall be in thine heart.

What is new is not the commandment. It is the hour — the darkness is past, and the true light now shineth. The light is new; the commandment it shines on is as old as the covenant. There is nothing new in the New Testament; here the New Testament says so.$card$, '{"Deuteronomy 6:5-6","Leviticus 19:18","1 John 2:7-8"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
