INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = '1-john' AND c.chapter_number = 5 AND v.verse_number = 3), 'teaching', 'The teaching', 'His commandments are not grievous — not hidden, not far off, very nigh', $card$*For this is the love of Elohim (God), that we keep his commandments: and his commandments are not grievous.* (1 John 5:3)

*For this commandment which I command thee this day, it is not hidden from thee, neither is it far off. It is not in heaven, that thou shouldest say, Who shall go up for us to heaven, and bring it unto us, that we may hear it, and do it? Neither is it beyond the sea, that thou shouldest say, Who shall go over the sea for us, and bring it unto us, that we may hear it, and do it? But the word is very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart, that thou mayest do it.* (Deuteronomy 30:11-14)

Not grievous is Moses' own assessment, restated. The commandment is not hidden, not far off, not in heaven, not beyond the sea — it is very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart, that thou mayest do it. The apostle and the Torah give the same verdict on the same commandments.

The inherited reading was handed a different verdict — the commandments as a burden grace removes. But the two witnesses on the page agree against it: keeping his commandments is what the love of Elohim (God) is, and the commandments themselves were given near and light.$card$, '{"Deuteronomy 30:11-14","1 John 5:3"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
