INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'revelation' AND c.chapter_number = 11 AND v.verse_number = 15), 'kingdom', 'The kingdom', 'The kingdoms of this world are become — the stone the prophets saw', $card$*And the seventh angel sounded; and there were great voices in heaven, saying, The kingdoms of this world are become the kingdoms of our Lord, and of his Messiah (Christ); and he shall reign for ever and ever.* (Revelation 11:15)

*And in the days of these kings shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed: and the kingdom shall not be left to other people, but it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever.* (Daniel 2:44)

*And Yahuah (LORD) shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one Yahuah (LORD), and his name one.* (Zechariah 14:9)

The seventh trumpet announces nothing the prophets had not already announced. Daniel saw the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom which shall never be destroyed, breaking in pieces all the kingdoms of men. Zechariah saw the day when Yahuah (God) shall be king over all the earth — one Yahuah (God), and his name one.

The great voices in heaven are quoting their own scriptures. The kingdom proclaimed through the whole good news is this kingdom — declared from the beginning, standing for ever, and his reign for ever and ever.$card$, '{"Daniel 2:44","Zechariah 14:9","Revelation 11:15"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
