INSERT INTO kingdom_verses (verse_id, strand, strand_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'revelation' AND c.chapter_number = 19 AND v.verse_number = 9), 'good_news', 'The good news', 'The marriage supper of the Lamb — the forsaken wife gathered home', $card$*Let us be glad and rejoice, and give honour to him: for the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made herself ready. And to her was granted that she should be arrayed in fine linen, clean and white: for the fine linen is the righteousness of saints. And he saith unto me, Write, Blessed are they which are called unto the marriage supper of the Lamb. And he saith unto me, These are the true sayings of Elohim (God).* (Revelation 19:7-9)

*For Yahuah (LORD) hath called thee as a woman forsaken and grieved in spirit, and a wife of youth, when thou wast refused, saith thy Elohim (God). For a small moment have I forsaken thee; but with great mercies will I gather thee.* (Isaiah 54:6-7)

*And it shall be at that day, saith Yahuah (LORD), that thou shalt call me Ishi; and shalt call me no more Baali.* (Hosea 2:16)

The wife at the marriage of the Lamb is not a bride from nowhere. The prophets know her history: a woman forsaken and grieved in spirit, a wife of youth who was refused — forsaken a small moment, and gathered with great mercies. The gathering and the marriage are the same mercy; the supper is the homecoming feast.

Hosea heard the day named: thou shalt call me Ishi — my husband — and call me no more Baali. The cast-off wife restored to her husband is the oldest love story in the prophets, and Revelation 19 is its wedding day.$card$, '{"Isaiah 54:6-7","Hosea 2:16","Revelation 19:7-9"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
